 $\boxed{}$. The absolute value of a complex number a + $\mathrm bi$ is given by $\left|{a+\mathrm bi}\right|=\sqrt{\mathrm{a}^2+\mathrm{b}^2}$.

For the given complex number $-4+\frac{7}{6}i$, we substitute $a=-4$ and $b=\frac{7}{6}$ into the formula:

\begin{align} 
\left|{-4+\frac{7}{6}i}\right| &= \sqrt{\left(-4\right)^2+\left(\frac{7}{6}\right)^2} \\
&= \sqrt{16+\frac{49}{36}} \\
&= \sqrt{\frac{576+49}{36}} \\
&= \sqrt{\frac{625}{36}} \\
&= \frac{25}{6} \\
\boxed{} &= \frac{25}{6}
\end{align}
